Subject: [PATCH v11 05/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Sync the list both ways
 with Fastmail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: llrnrlvxupkmxyzxwrttskqynyvozqus
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:21:15 +0000

A one-way fetch makes lab-mail a copy of Fastmail. A move or
deletion made on lab-mail never reaches Fastmail, and one made on
Fastmail never reaches lab-mail. Syncing both ways, with Archive
beside INBOX, lets either side change the list while Fastmail still
keeps every message.

- mbsync syncs INBOX and Archive both ways, and no other folder, but
  never expunges or removes. A message expunged on one side is only
  marked \Deleted on the other.
- mbsync creates Archive on Dovecot from Fastmail's, and its login
  gains the ACL's create right, so Fastmail alone decides which
  folders exist. Dovecot only marks Archive \Archive.
- The fetch job becomes the sync job, with its own log and stamp.
